From 27ad23005d559ec7c0a778ec298de99d03a1d78b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:22:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 114/115] R6's engine hooks: a native present, the flip gate, a
 benchmark mode, native reports and guest reads

For a native renderer that draws every frame itself (the port's
docs/NATIVE_R6.md), development only, inert unless a host asks:
- rsx_vk_bridge_present_prepare / _submit / _cancel: the host blits its
  frame into the present's offscreen target on its own queue, and the
  present's submission waits on its semaphore; the window present stays
  on the host's present thread;
- cellGcm_set_flip_gate: a flip completes only once the host has
  executed it too; cellGcm_set_flip_immediate (benchmarks): a flip
  completes when executed, not at the next vblank tick;
- PS3RECOMP_VK_PRESENT_MODE=mailbox|immediate (benchmarks; FIFO when the
  surface has none) and PS3RECOMP_VK_READBACK=0 (no per-frame copy to host
  memory);
- a bridge signal asked for with nothing recorded in the open command
  buffer is submitted alone at once (it orders after everything submitted
  before it): attached, it waited for an engine submission that never came
  once the engine drew nothing -- the native side waiting on it and the
  walker on the native side;
- cellGcm_title_context_pub, cellGcm_display_buffer_pub,
  cellGcm_report_write_pub / _copy_pub / _timestamp_pub, cellGcm_io2ea_pub;
  cellGcm_set_guest_read_hook (a host holding a surface's newest content
  reads it into guest memory for the JPEG and PNG encoders);
- occlusionQueryPrecise enabled on the device when it has it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
